diff --git a/docs/deployment.md b/docs/deployment.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9b701ff
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/deployment.md
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+# Deploy Fizzy on one server with Kamal
+
+Point a public DNS hostname at your Linux server. Allow inbound HTTP and HTTPS
+(ports 80 and 443) for Kamal Proxy to obtain and renew its TLS certificate.
+You need SSH access (root by default, or set `ssh.user` in the config) and
+Docker on the server. On your deploying machine, install Docker with Buildx,
+use the Ruby version in `.ruby-version`, and run `bundle install` in your fork.
+
+1. Edit `config/deploy.yml`: replace `fizzy.example.com` with your hostname
+   (no scheme or path). Set `SMTP_ADDRESS`, `SMTP_PORT` and `MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS`
+   for your mail provider; use a sender it authorizes. The example uses SMTP
+   submission with STARTTLS on port 587. For an ARM server, set `builder.arch`
+   to `arm64` instead of `amd64`.
+2. Copy `.kamal/secrets.example` to `.kamal/secrets`. Paste the output of
+   `bin/rails secret` into `SECRET_KEY_BASE` and enter the SMTP credentials.
+   Keep this file private and retain the same key for future deploys. For a
+   relay without authentication, remove `SMTP_USERNAME` and `SMTP_PASSWORD`
+   from `env.secret`.
+3. Commit your config changes (not your secrets) and run `bin/kamal setup`.
+   Open `https://your-hostname` and sign up with your email address. Receiving
+   the sign-in code checks both background processing and mail delivery.
+
+For updates, commit your changes and run `bin/kamal deploy`. The app container
+runs both Puma and Solid Queue. Its named Docker volume `fizzy_storage` holds
+all SQLite databases and uploaded files under `/rails/storage`, and is reused
+when the container is replaced. Keep the volume name unchanged and back it up;
+a volume protects against container replacement, not disk failure.
+
+To enable browser push notifications, [generate a VAPID key pair](development.md#web-push-notifications)
+and add `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` and `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` to both `.kamal/secrets`
+(values) and `env.secret` (names only) before deploying.
